Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hako-base
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 systemd,
 util-linux,
 gdisk,
 cloud-guest-utils,
 e2fsprogs
Description: hako base system
 System parts of hako that do not depend on the board or the session:
  - on the first boot, grow the data partition (file system label "data")
    to the end of the disk (hako-grow-data.service), so a small image can be
    written to any bigger card

Package: hako-session
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 hako-base,
 systemd,
 libpam-systemd,
 dbus,
 pipewire,
 wireplumber,
 pipewire-alsa,
 cage,
 wlr-randr,
 triggerhappy
Conflicts: rpmini-session
Replaces: rpmini-session, rpmini-bsp (<< 0.2.0)
Description: hako game session
 Starts the game application full screen on tty1 at boot as the
 unprivileged user "hako" and restarts it when it exits. The application
 is the /usr/bin/hako-app alternative (normally hako-launcher); app
 packages register themselves with update-alternatives.
 .
 Runs it in the kiosk compositor cage, rotated by HAKO_ROTATE for portrait
 panels. Board defaults come from /usr/lib/hako/session.d/*.sh of the board
 support package. Sound goes through PipeWire / WirePlumber in the session;
 the volume keys change the PipeWire volume (triggerhappy).

